2. Market data used in the underlying experiments
   - Study A minute bars: HF Data Library (US OHLCV), e.g. Hugging Face dataset
     “elkassabgi/hfdatalibrary” and related vendor feeds. Users must obtain data
     under the dataset/vendor terms.
   - Study B minute bars: Binance USDT spot klines (experiment-host inventory).
     Users must obtain data under Binance terms. Not redistributed here.
   - The original Jiang–Kelly–Xiu study uses CRSP daily equity data (not redistributed).
   CRSP is a product of the Center for Research in Security Prices, University of Chicago.

3. Open-source code references (inspiration / comparison; not claimed as our work)
   - https://github.com/gaoym4321/ReImagining_Price_Trends
   - https://github.com/lich99/Stock_CNN
   Those repositories retain their own licenses. Review them before reuse.

This repository ships experimental reports, tables, protocol freezes, and small
pure-Python snapshots (equity bar transforms; crypto formation/metrics/execution
helpers). It does not ship CRSP data, full 1-minute archives, image tensors,
checkpoints, official paper image packs, or third-party model weights.
